  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef's robot starts from the coordinate (0,0)(0, 0)(0,0) and wishes to reach to the coordinate (N,M)(N, M)(N,M).\n\nThe initial energy of the robot is 000. There are KKK `batteries` kept at some of the coordinates such that picking up the ithi^{th}ith `battery` costs CiC_iCi​ units, and, on picking the ithi^{th}ith `battery`, the current energy of the robot becomes EiE_iEi​.\n\nNote that one coordinate can have multiple `batteries` but the robot can pick **at most one** `battery` out of those.\n\nFor example, if the robot reaches a certain coordinate with energy AAA and there are two batteries with energy B1B_1B1​ and B2B_2B2​ on that coordinate, the robot may choose at most one battery out of these. On choosing the first battery, the energy of the robot becomes B1B_1B1​ (not A+B1A+B_1A+B1​).\n\nThe robot can walk in all the four directions as follows:\n\n\nMove up:  Moving from coordinate (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) to (X,Y+1)(X, Y+1)(X,Y+1), the robot **loses** 111 unit of energy.\nMove down: Moving from coordinate (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) to (X,Y−1)(X, Y-1)(X,Y−1), the robot **gains** 111 unit of energy.\nMove right: Moving from coordinate (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) to (X+1,Y)(X+1, Y)(X+1,Y), the robot **loses** 111 unit of energy.\nMove left: Moving from coordinate (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) to (X−1,Y)(X-1, Y)(X−1,Y), the robot **gains** 111 unit of energy.\nFind the **minimum** cost to reach (N,M)(N, M)(N,M) if the robot maintains a **non-negative** energy throughout the journey (including the destination).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer&nbsp;TTT, the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows.\nEach test cases consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains three positive integers N,M,N, M,N,M, and KKK, the coordinates of the destination and the number of batteries.\nNext KKK lines have four space-separated integers each: Xi,Yi,Ci,EiX_i, Y_i, C_i, E_iXi​,Yi​,Ci​,Ei​. The ithi^{th}ith line indicates that the coordinate (Xi,Yi)(X_i, Y_i)(Xi​,Yi​) has a `battery` with cost CiC_iCi​ and energy EiE_iEi​.\n\n\n**The input data guarantees that the robot can reach the destination.**\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer, the **minimum** cost from (0,0)(0,0)(0,0) to (N,M)(N, M)(N,M).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤K≤1051 \\leq K \\leq 10^51≤K≤105",
      "0≤Xi,Yi≤2∗1090 \\leq X_i,Y_i \\leq 2*10^90≤Xi​,Yi​≤2∗109",
      "1≤N,M,Ci,Ei≤2∗1091 \\leq N,M,C_i,E_i \\leq 2*10^91≤N,M,Ci​,Ei​≤2∗109",
      "The sum of KKK over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5 5 3\n0 0 10 10\n0 0 2 4\n2 2 1 1\n5 5 4\n0 0 10 10\n0 0 2 4\n2 2 1 1\n4 1 3 5",
        "output": "10\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Use the first battery with cost 101010. Thus, at coordinate (0,0)(0, 0)(0,0), the energy of the robot becomes 101010 units. The robot can traverse the path :(0,0)−(0,1)−…−(0,5)−(1,5)−…−(5,5)(0,0) - (0, 1) - \\ldots - (0, 5) - (1, 5) - \\ldots - (5,5)(0,0)−(0,1)−…−(0,5)−(1,5)−…−(5,5). It can be shown that the robot cannot reach the destination in less than 101010 units cost.\nTest case 222:\n\nUse the 2nd2^{nd}2nd battery: At coordinate (0,0)(0, 0)(0,0), robot picks the 2nd2^{nd}2nd battery and the energy of the robot becomes 444 units. The robot can move to coordinate (2,2)(2, 2)(2,2) using this energy. On reaching (2,2)(2, 2)(2,2), robot's energy is 000.\nUse the 3rd3^{rd}3rd battery: At coordinate (2,2)(2, 2)(2,2), robot picks the 3rd3^{rd}3rd battery and the energy of the robot becomes 111 unit. The robot can move from (2,2)(2, 2)(2,2) to (2,1)(2, 1)(2,1) and gain 111 unit of energy. Thus, it has 222 units of energy now. It can now move from (2,1)(2, 1)(2,1) to (4,1)(4, 1)(4,1) using this energy.\nUse the 4th4^{th}4th battery: At coordinate (4,1)(4, 1)(4,1), robot picks the 4th4^{th}4th battery and the energy of the robot becomes 555 units. The robot can now move from (4,1)(4, 1)(4,1) to (5,5)(5, 5)(5,5)."
      }
    ]
  },
